<h3 id="help-in-german">Help in German</h3>

<p>The full help book is translated: the in-app Help window and the pages at <a href="https://markedapp.com/help">markedapp.com/help</a>. Section titles, the sidebar, and the topic pages are in German. A handful of license pages stay in English, because those texts are the upstream licenses and I did not rewrite them.</p>

<p>A huge thanks to <strong>Thomas Heinrichsdobler</strong> for the German translation.</p>

<h3 id="it-picks-the-language-for-you">It picks the language for you</h3>

<p>On the web, a German browser opens the German help. The English pages live at addresses like <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">https://markedapp.com/help/Overview</code>. The German pages live under <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">/help/de/</code>, so the same topic is <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">https://markedapp.com/help/de/Overview</code>. The flag buttons at the top of the page switch between them and remember the choice in the browser. After that, the saved choice wins over the browser language.</p>

<p>In the app, Help follows the language macOS is using. A Mac set to German opens the German help book. The same flags sit at the top of the Help window. Pick one and Marked remembers it, so you can read the English help on a German Mac, or the other way around. If a page has no German file, that page stays in English instead of showing a blank window.</p>

<h3 id="translators-wanted">Translators wanted</h3>

<p>German is the first language I have ready to ship. The other help locales already exist as machine-translated drafts for the most part. They need people who can read them, fix the wording in their own language, and line the terms up with the app. I am offering an hourly rate plus free licenses for that work.</p>

<p>The drafts are in the help source repository: <a href="https://github.com/ttscoff/marked-docs">github.com/ttscoff/marked-docs</a>. English is the root of that repo. Each language has its own folder.</p>

<p>I am looking for translators for:</p>

